A simple decorator I often use is a timer that measures how long a method call takes and returns the results. This is useful when building prototypes that call different models—with varying latencies—to check the time taken for each call.

```
from functools import wraps
from time import perf_counter
from typing import Callable
from typing import Tuple

def timer(func: Callable) -> Callable:
 @wraps(func)
 def wrapper(*args, kwargs):
 start = perf_counter()
 results = func(*args, kwargs)
 end = perf_counter()
 run_time = end - start
 return results, run_time

 return wrapper

@timer
def predict_with_time(model, X_test: np.array) -> Tuple[np.array]:
 return model.predict(X_test)
```
